# config/env.example
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY NOTICE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is a template.  Copy it to config/env and fill in your real keys.
# config/env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Usage
# ─────
# Source manually before running the listener or CLI:
#   source config/env
#   crew-chief listen --config config/listener/config.toml
#   crew-chief agent "how much disk space is free?" --tools shell
#
# The run scripts (scripts/run_listener.sh, scripts/start_listener.sh) source
# this file automatically when it exists, so systemd and background invocations
# pick up the keys without any extra steps.
#
# Which keys are needed
# ──────────────────────
# Only export the keys for providers you have listed in
# config/listener/config.toml → llm.fallback_chain.
# Keys for providers not in your chain are never read.
#
#   fallback_chain = ["ollama", "claude-cli", "codex-cli", "anthropic", "openai"]
#   ↑ ollama / claude-cli / codex-cli need no key — authenticated separately
#   ↑ anthropic → set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   ↑ openai    → set OPENAI_API_KEY

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key
# Required when "anthropic" is in your fallback_chain.
# Obtain at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI API key
# Required when "openai" is in your fallback_chain.
# Obtain at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# export OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-..."
